## Vercel Web Analytics Integration

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js 14 project following the official Vercel documentation.

### Changes Made:

**Modified Files:**

1. **frontend/app/layout.tsx**
   - Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
   - Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the body element in the root layout
   - Preserved all existing structure, metadata, and styling

2. **frontend/package.json**
   - Added dependency: `@vercel/analytics` (version ^2.0.1)

3. **frontend/package-lock.json**
   - Updated to include @vercel/analytics and its 394 new dependencies

### Implementation Details:

- **Framework**: Next.js 14.2.15 with App Router
- **Package Manager**: npm
- **Analytics Package**: @vercel/analytics@^2.0.1
- **Installation Method**: Followed official Vercel documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart

The Analytics component is placed within the body element of the root layout (app/layout.tsx), which is the recommended approach for Next.js App Router projects. This ensures analytics tracking is active across all pages of the application.

### Verification Completed:

✅ Build successful - Next.js production build completed without errors
✅ Linting passed - No ESLint warnings or errors
✅ Type checking passed - TypeScript compilation successful with no type errors
✅ Package dependencies installed and lock file updated

### Next Steps:

Deploy the application to Vercel to activate the analytics tracking. Analytics data will be available in the Vercel dashboard after deployment.
